A pass that ends with a plan for later work leaves that work undone,
because nothing runs between passes; it waits until Pat writes again
and asks why nothing happened. When a pass truly cannot finish, a bare
status report gives him nothing to decide. Naming what is needed, or
the options with their costs and a recommendation, lets one reply from
him unblock the work.
